    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1896-98/document/80> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/420766166/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Tuesday March 2. 1897. Fiesole. Villa Rosa 
A miserable day for me owing to Bernhard’s losing his temper several times while working with me in the morning, and simply furiously in the afternoon because he thought I was cheated by the men who brought a book from the Railway. Perhaps I was, but it is scarcely worth making a disgusting scene about. I feel very miserable over it – such things upset me terribly – and if he is like this now, what  will  he be as an old man? It isn’t a  deep  fault, but it is perhaps more wearing than a really worse thing would be. Eheu! """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 80 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1896-98> .

